== Classification of DEs

An *ODE* includes derivitives with one variable, while a *PDE* includes more
than one variable.

An n-th order *linear* ODE has the general form:

$ a_n y^(\(n\)) + a_(n-1) y^(\(n-1\)) + ... + a_0 y(x) = f(x) $

Where $a_n, a_(n-1), ..., f(x)$ are functions of $x$. If $f(x) = 0$ then the ODE
is *homogenous*, else the ODE is *non-homogenous*.

=== Principle of Superstition

If $y = y_1(x)$ and $y = y_2(x)$ are particular solutions to a linear homogenous
ODE, then so is $y = A y_1 (x) + B y_2 (x)$ for any constants $A, B$.

